sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch15-06> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-06--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-06--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch15-06: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.51" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.514"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.64"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Egg outlines sufficient to compute the two principal curvatures are available for most bird families. The equation also contains external pressure, membrane tension, and internal pressure, none of which are measured, and if tension and external pressure may vary freely the equation is the equilibrium condition of a membrane rather than a restrictive law. A test with predeclared constraints on those fields is feasible and only partly identifies the equation Thompson calls the equation of all eggs." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: For measured egg profiles, solve p_n + T(1/r + 1/r′) = P under an explicit constraint on tension and external pressure, and compare residuals with purely geometric oval equations. The physical equation is supported only if a constrained pressure and tension field fits and the unconstrained alternative does not; with T and p_n both free, essentially any axisymmetric egg can be made to satisfy the equation." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Internal pressure and membrane tension during shell formation are not in any of the shape archives.", "A free tension function can absorb almost any smooth profile, which makes an unconstrained fit uninformative." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch15-06--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch15-06--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch15-06--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-06--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch15-06 by Grok 4.7: 0.5" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.5"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-06--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch15-06> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-06--grok--operationalizability> .
